# Multi-target release rule (Meet Map)

Meet Map ships as **four targets** that must stay in sync:

- **Mobile web app**: `C:\Users\areil\Documents\meetmap` (Vercel alias `meetmap-gilt.vercel.app`)
- **Desktop web app (findcarmeets.com)**: `C:\Users\areil\Documents\meetmap-desktop\meetmap-desktop` (Vercel alias `www.findcarmeets.com`)
- **Android app**: Capacitor project under `meetmap/android` built from the same web bundle
- **iOS app**: Capacitor project under `meetmap/ios` — on Mac, `npm run mac:arrival` or `npm run cap:sync` after pull; open with `npm run cap:open:ios`

## Hard rule

If a change affects user-visible behavior or shared business logic, **do not ship it to only one target**.
Apply an equivalent change to **mobile + desktop**, and run **`npm run cap:sync`** so **Android and iOS** native projects get the same bundle (Mac: automatic via `mac:arrival`).

## Release checklist (when the user implies "ship"/"done"/"live")

- **Mobile web (`meetmap`)**
  - Run: `npm run format:check`, `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build`
  - Commit + push
  - Deploy: `npx vercel deploy --prod --yes`

- **Desktop web (`meetmap-desktop`)**
  - Run: `npm run build`
  - Commit + push
  - Deploy: `npx vercel deploy --prod --yes` (must alias to `www.findcarmeets.com`)

- **Android + iOS (Capacitor)**
  - Sync web → native: `npm run cap:sync` (Windows before Android release; Mac via `mac:arrival` or manual)
  - **Android** — if publishing to Google Play: `npm run build:android` (or `build:android:nobump` when requested); bump `versionCode` if required
  - **iOS** — on Mac after `cap:sync`: `npm run cap:open:ios`, archive/upload from Xcode

## Notes

- If a change is intentionally target-specific, call that out explicitly in the final summary (e.g. “desktop-only SEO page change”).
- If any target cannot be updated (missing access, build failure, or other blocker), stop and report the blocker instead of partially shipping.

